@1 = ~A magnificent show. Truly. Alas, I must be off. You didn't actually expect me to share my reward with the likes of you, did you?~
@2 = ~I have nothing to say to you. Begone!~
@3 = ~Hmm...~
@4 = ~Long time no see. How long has it been? Ten months? A whole year?~
@5 = ~Cut it out, Safana. Time has not erased the troubles you caused aboard the Exzesus. Most notably your last stand, when you manipulated Captain Borsakov into submission and attempted to seize the helm, steering the ship according to your own whims.~
@6 = ~Count yourself lucky, Safana. Instead of making you seafood, I have a much more fitting resolution to satisfy my hunger for retaliation.~
@7 = ~I'll collect the bounty from your father in Calimport. He pays a round sum for bringing his daughter back home alive.~
@8 = ~Careful, Safana. He said alive. He didn't specify that you have to be in one piece. Wouldn't want your toys—oh, I meant friends—to be dead and your pretty face scarred now, would you?~
@9 = ~Keep barking, bitch, and someone will put you on a leash one day. Pray that this someone isn't me. As charismatic as you can be, I know your tricks and schemes. I've learned first-hand what it means to cross the infamous Safana the Charmer. Your rich father struggled to set you straight then, but I'm sure he can reform you.~
@10 = ~Whoa, whoa. All right. I do not wish to fight you. Look, you don't understand it. Safana fled her family to chase her desires for a better life. In order to achieve that life, she masks her narcissism beneath her charm and beauty. She's greedy, selfish, and acquisitive. She cannot be trusted! Mark my words.~
@11 = ~I urge you to reconsider.~
@12 = ~My decision stands. Safana stays with me.~
@13 = ~One woman is not worth losing your life over, and I implore you: you will lose it if you take one more step toward her.~
@14 = ~How about we both take her to Calimport? Surely we can share the bounty.~
@15 = ~Let Coran handle it.~
@16 = ~So? Will you help me or not?~
@17 = ~I know you would. Don't worry, I won't let him take you.~
@18 = ~You clearly wouldn't. But you're with us now, and I won't let him take you.~
@19 = ~Is the prospect of reuniting with your father really that bad?~
@20 = ~How about we both take her to Calimport? Surely we can share the bounty.~
@21 = ~Let Coran handle it.~
@22 = ~Then we are at an impasse. I may lack enough equipment and skill to match yours but believe me, one day I shall come back and Safana WILL be mine.~
@23 = ~Then we are at an impasse. I may lack enough equipment and skill to match yours but believe me, one day I shall come back and Safana WILL be mine.~
@24 = ~Betraying your own for the sake of money? Ha! You could make a formidable pirate yourself had we still had a need for recruits. Devious.~
@25 = ~As long as I am present in this group, Safana will not be held accountable for misdeeds she committed in the past. People make mistakes, and that does not make them any less worthy of redemption. We are standing in Baldur's Gate, where opportunities for bounties and merchandise are endless. You want to claim a bounty? There are plenty more to choose from, for possibly equal material rewards. Would it hurt that much to look past this one?~
@26 = ~Hmm. You make some good points, elf. Safana and I have a rather... complicated history, but I might overlook that. See, we are alike, wouldn't you say, Safana?~
@27 = ~With pleasure. May I never see you again, Safana.~
@28 = ~Let's back up and take a longer route around. Way longer route.~
@29 = ~Balthrim! How pleasurable it is to see you again.~
@30 = ~I am a woman of unequivocal tastes, Balthrim. I can't help that my desires are a slight bit over-dominant. You wouldn't let it slide after all that time?~
@31 = ~Oh, darling. All you had to do was ask straight away...~
@32 = ~My... what? That old buffoon is still looking for me? You will not take me back there. My new friends won't let you.~
@33 = ~Whatever my father claims to pay, I can pay you more. Like old times, remember? Bribes were but a delight for you. You'd gladly accept them from just about anyone who was willing. Gold... or other favours you could seek with my company, handsome.~
@34 = ~Help me this instant! I am your partner for life and death, am I not? I would do the same for you. You know that, right?~
@35 = ~I know you would. Don't worry, I won't let him take you.~
@36 = ~You clearly wouldn't. But you're with us now, and I won't let him take you.~
@37 = ~Is the prospect of reuniting with your father really that bad?~
@38 = ~How about we both take her to Calimport? Surely we can share the bounty.~
@39 = ~Let Coran handle it.~
@40 = ~Nonsense. I am naturally eye-pleasing, and I don't shy away from it. Neither do I shy away from being open about my cravings. What kind of person would I be if I hid my intentions rather than embraced them, and expected the same from my fellows and... bedfellows?~
@41 = ~My hero. See, Balthrim? My new henchman is ready to throw you across the sea, back to Maztica where you came from. Consider that your final warning to back off.~
@42 = ~My father is a pompous scion who restricted me. He played the part of the overprotective father rather well. Had me locked within four bland walls of my room and kept insisting that every restriction was for my own good. My wants, my wishes, never came to pass under his watchful eye because he attempted to instil in me the belief that the outside world was cruel and vile.~
@43 = ~He was right about that much. The world is full of nasty surprises. If you do not wish to be swallowed by its darkness, you learn to adapt to it. You assimilate. You survive. By whatever means necessary.~
@44 = ~You will NOT take me alive!~
@45 = ~Not in the least, darling. You've been given a chance to walk away. Do so now.~
@46 = ~You will NOT take me alive!~
@47 = ~As long as I am present in this group, Safana will not be held accountable for misdeeds she committed in the past. People make mistakes, and that does not make them any less worthy of redemption. We are standing in Baldur's Gate, where opportunities for bounties and merchandise are endless. You want to claim a bounty? There are plenty more to choose from, for possibly equal material rewards. Would it hurt that much to look past this one?~
@48 = ~I expected better of you. Since you are not the person I thought you were, I shall take my leave now. Selling our companions out for profit should be beneath us, and I will have nothing to do with it!~
